# Windows script files must keep CRLF endings on checkout.
#
# cmd.exe parses a .bat line by line as it runs it, and a label or a goto that
# ends in a bare LF can be misread - which produces the worst kind of failure,
# one that works on one machine and silently jumps to the wrong place on
# another. Nothing about that is obvious from reading the file, so it is
# pinned here rather than left to whatever core.autocrlf happens to be set to.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Icons are binary; never touch them.
*.ico  binary
